# Public repository boundary: production state and credentials never belong here.
#
# Deny everything, then allow only the reviewed public tree. Keep it that way:
# every new public file goes under public/, never at the repository root.
#
# Do NOT add a bare "!README.md". A pattern with no slash matches at any depth,
# so it un-ignores the ROOT README.md — the internal operator hub that names the
# cluster layout and the ~/.secrets/home-lab credential inventory path. That one
# line is what made "git add ." unsafe. public/README.md is already covered by
# the public/ rules below and needs no exception of its own.
*
!.gitignore
!public/
!public/**
